      <div type="clause" n="69">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:IICn">II Cn</ref> 69</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="69" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="356" ed="#liebermann"/>Þis is þonne seo<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#IICn_69.lnote.oe.1-4"/> lihtingc<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#IICn_69.lnote.oe.2-3"/>, þe ic<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#IICn_69.lnote.oe.1-4"/> wylle eallon folce gebeorgan, þe hig ær þyson<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#IICn_69.lnote.oe.3-2"/> mid gedrehte<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#IICn_69.lnote.oe.4"/> wæran ealles to swyðe.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="69" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="356" ed="#liebermann"/>Ðis is ðonne se<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#IICn_69.lnote.oe.1-2"/> lihtingc, ðe ic wylle eallon folce gebeorgan, ðe hig ær ðyson mid gedrehte wæron ealles to swyðe.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="69" corresp="#wit-a"><pb n="356" ed="#liebermann"/>Þis is þonne lihtingc<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#IICn_69.lnote.oe.1-5"/>, þe wille eallon folce gebeorgan, þe hig ær þysson mid gedrehte wæron ealles to swiðe.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="69" corresp="#wit-q"><ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#IICn_69.lnote.oe.1-3"/><pb n="357" ed="#liebermann"/>Hęc est igitur<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#IICn_69.lnote.oe.2-2"/> alleuiatio, quam<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#IICn_69.lnote.oe.3"/> omni populo meo preuideri uolo, in quibus nimis omnino fuerant aggrauati.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="69" corresp="#wit-inst-cn"><pb n="357" ed="#liebermann"/>Hęc<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#IICn_69.lnote.oe.1-6"/> est alleuiatio, quam ego uolo fieri<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#IICn_69.lnote.oe.2-4"/> omni populo, unde<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#IICn_69.lnote.oe.3-3"/> hactenus ultra modum fuerunt grauati.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="69" corresp="#wit-cons-cn"><pb n="357" ed="#liebermann"/>De libertatibus post concessis. Hoc est autem alleuamen, quod uniuerse genti mee parcere uolo, a quibus ante hec nimium erant g[rau]ati.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#robertson" n="69" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="208" ed="#robertson"/>Ðis is ðonne se lihtingc ðe ic wylle eallon folce gebeorgan, ðe hig ær ðyson mid gedrehte wæron ealles to swyðe.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="288" ed="#rabin-doml"/>Þis is þonne seo lihtingc þe ic wylle eallon folce gebeorgan, þe hig ær þyson mid gedrehte wæran ealles to swyðe.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="356" ed="#liebermann"/>Folgendes<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#IICn_69.lnote.de.1"/> ist nun die Erleichterung, wodurch ich<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#IICn_69.lnote.de.2"/> allem Volke Schutz gewähren will [dávor], womit sie bisher allzu sehr bedrückt gewesen sind.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">The following, now, is the relief by which I wish to give all the people protection [against that] with which they have hitherto been all too greatly oppressed.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="209" ed="#robertson"/>Now this is the mitigation by means of which I desire to protect the general public in cases where, until now, they have been far too greatly oppressed.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#whitelock"><pb n="472" ed="#whitelock"/>Now this is the mitigation by which I wish to protect all the people from what they were hitherto oppressed with all too greatly.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="289" ed="#rabin-doml"/>Accordingly, this is the mitigation by which I mean to protect the people in cases where they previously were all too greatly oppressed.</ab>
        <note type="editorial">Liebermann suggests correcting A to ‘seo lihtingc, þe ic wille’.; BR: added from Gesetze I p. 357, October 2026 (MS Cons)</note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_69.lnote.oe.1" n="1" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">357</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-si <hi rend="italic">Hr</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-si Hr</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_69.lnote.oe.2" n="2" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">357</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">nimirum e. gl'ati <hi rend="italic">Hr</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">nimirum e. gl'ati Hr</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_69.lnote.oe.1-2" n="1" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">356</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">s. o.</hi> 23,1 <hi rend="italic">Hs. A</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">see above 23,1 MS A</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_69.lnote.oe.1-3" n="1" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">357</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Leges Cnuti regis <hi rend="italic">roth R</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Leges Cnuti regis in red R</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_69.lnote.oe.2-2" n="2" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">357</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">fehlt KHk</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">lacking in KHk</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_69.lnote.oe.3" n="3" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">357</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">qua <hi rend="italic">K</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">qua K</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_69.lnote.oe.1-4" n="1" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">356</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">fehlt Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">lacking in Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_69.lnote.oe.2-3" n="2" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">356</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-ge, de wille <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-ge, de wille Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_69.lnote.oe.3-2" n="3" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">356</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">ðysson <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">ðysson Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_69.lnote.oe.4" n="4" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">356</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-ht wæron e. to swiþe <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-ht wæron e. to swiþe Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_69.lnote.oe.1-5" n="1" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">356</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">bessere</hi> seo l., þe ic</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">read seo l., þe ic</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_69.lnote.oe.1-6" n="1" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">357</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Hęc — grau. <hi rend="italic">roth Lb S</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Hęc — grau. in red Lb S</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_69.lnote.oe.2-4" n="2" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">357</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">übergeschr. H; fehlt DiLbJo;</hi> o. p. f. <hi rend="italic">CbRl</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">written above in H; lacking in DiLbJo; o. p. f. CbRl</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_69.lnote.oe.3-3" n="3" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">357</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">ut nullatenus sint <hi rend="italic">Lb S Jo</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">ut nullatenus sint Lb S Jo</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IICn_69.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">211</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Das Folgende bis 74 bildet Einen Abschnitt nach Kemble <hi rend="italic">Saxons</hi> II 96. 164. Mir scheint nur 69—71, 5 zusammenhängend die Beschränkung fiskalischer bzw. gefolgsherrlicher Willkür zu bringen</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">According to Kemble <hi rend="italic">Saxons</hi> II 96. 164, what follows, up to 74, forms a single section. To me only 69—71, 5 seem to belong together, dealing with the restriction of arbitrary exactions by the fisc or by lords of retainers</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IICn_69.lnote.de.2" n="2" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">211</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Offenbar spricht hier ein volksfreundlich gesinnter Herrscher persönlich; <hi rend="italic">s. o</hi>. Einl. 21</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Evidently a ruler well disposed towards the people is speaking here in person; <hi rend="italic">see above</hi> Introduction 21</seg></note>
      </div>
